meta {
  name: List a server’s alert rules
  type: http
  seq: 69
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/cloud-servers/:cloudServer_id/alert-rules
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  cloudServer_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Every alert in the catalogue for this server, each marked as inherited from the organization, overridden here or not configured, with `fired_30d`: how many incidents it raised on this server in the last 30 days. Older standalone rules are listed apart, and `workloads` lists the rules that watch one service or container, each with its `target` (`kind`, `match` — a service’s unit, or a container’s main program and lowest published port — and `name`), `threshold` (restarts within `restart_window_minutes` that count as a loop) and `duration_minutes` (how long it may be stopped). With `active=1` it returns only the rules actually being evaluated, as a flat list.

  Scope: `cloud.read`
}
